<title>USA: LSB Industries buys Oklahoma City building.</title>
<headline>LSB Industries buys Oklahoma City building.</headline>
<dateline>OKLAHOMA CITY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>LSB Industries Inc on Tuesday said its Prime Financial Corp subsidiary acquired The Tower, a 22-storey office building in Oklahoma City, for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The building, with 293,096 square feet of space, formerly housed Equity Bank, an LSB subsidiary that was sold in 1994. LSB retained an option to purchase the building.</p>
<p>The company, which makes chemicals and air conditioning products, expects the building to increase in value this year and provide cash flow.</p>
<p>	 ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
